---
title: Seated Single-Leg Forward Fold
type: docs
prev: docs/rastyazhka/
---
![наклон к ноге сидя](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/316a39c5-320e-4457-8f2f-05d471fa790b)

{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Sit on the floor with both legs stretched straight out in front of you.

### Step 2
Bend your left knee and place the sole of your left foot against your inner right thigh.

### Step 3
Hinge forward at your hips toward your straight right leg, reaching for your foot or shin with both hands.

### Step 4
Keep your back flat rather than rounding your lower back, feeling a stretch along your hamstring, calf, and inner thigh.

### Step 5
Hold this position for the recommended amount of time (usually 15–30 seconds).

### Step 6
Switch legs and repeat the stretch on the other side.

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
• Try to keep the target muscles relaxed during the stretch.

• Breathe slowly and steadily.

• Do not force the stretch—stretch only until you feel comfortable tension, never sharp pain.
{{< /callout >}}
